/target

# what a local run of the agent leaves in the working directory: the settings its harness writes,
# and the sandbox's scratch directory when a confined command was killed before it could be tidied
.claude/settings.local.json
kamchatka-*/

# what `cargo run --example recorded` writes: whole sessions, regenerated on demand
recorded/

# where proptest writes the seed of a case that failed. Deliberately not tracked, against
# proptest's own advice: a failure worth keeping is worth reading, and every test in this
# workspace is a sentence with a note saying what was wrong. The discipline is to lift a
# counterexample into a named case with that note and let the property go on guarding the class -
# a file of opaque hashes is the shape of a regression suite nobody can read, and half of these
# are seeds for implementations that no longer exist.
**/proptest-regressions/
**/*.proptest-regressions

# rustfmt's backups and the counters a profiled run drops
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw

# documents that belong to another repository and only ever pass through this working directory.
# A pattern rather than a name, because the point is that no such file is ever committed here by
# accident - and because the local `.git/info/exclude` that has been holding the line is not
# shared, so a fresh clone somewhere else has nothing stopping a `git add -A`
*.pdf

# editors and desktops
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
